noVNC: QEMU VNC audio playback (pseudo-encoding -259), playback only.

Adapted from novnc/noVNC#1952 "Qemu audio support v2" by Dietmar Maurer
(https://github.com/novnc/noVNC/pull/1952, MPL-2.0; still open upstream).
This adaptation is MPL-2.0 like the rest of noVNC (see LICENSE.txt).

Changes from the upstream PR:
- -259 is advertised only when RFB is constructed with
  `options.audioContext`; without it the client behaves exactly as before.
- On the acknowledgement it requests S16 (format 3), 2 channels, 44100 Hz,
  then enables audio, once per connection.
- Audio messages arriving without a negotiated acknowledgement, and unknown
  QEMU sub-messages or operations, fail the connection.
- Zero-length data messages are tolerated (upstream stalls on them), and a
  data length above 1 MiB fails the connection.
- Playback runs in an AudioWorklet with a bounded jitter buffer: it starts
  after 60 ms is buffered, holds at most 100 ms, drops frames that arrive
  while it is full, and re-primes after an underrun. core/audio.js is both
  the page-side player and the worklet module, so it loads same-origin under
  script-src 'self'.
- No app/ui.js or vnc.html changes: the qrab console pages own the toggle.

qrab keeps two identical vendored copies. Apply to each with:
  git apply --directory=projects/bmc/assets/novnc contrib/novnc-audio.patch
  git apply --directory=projects/dashboard/assets/novnc contrib/novnc-audio.patch

